From 8418e69c13cf7fa28f8090ef765211190a166852 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Zhu, Yi" <chuyee@google.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:18:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kprobes: Propagate arm_kprobe() error in __register_kprobe()

Commit 587e8e6d640b ("kprobes: Adopt guard() and scoped_guard()")
replaced the 'goto out; ... return ret;' error path in __register_kprobe()
with an unconditional 'return 0;', causing __register_kprobe() to silently
drop the error returned by arm_kprobe().

When arm_kprobe() fails (for example, with -EBUSY when registering a
kprobe with a post_handler on a function already patched by livepatch,
due to an FTRACE_OPS_FL_IPMODIFY conflict), the probe is removed from
kprobe_table, try_to_optimize_kprobe() is called on the unlinked probe,
and 0 is returned to the caller as though registration succeeded.

This unintentionally reverted commit 12310e343755 ("kprobes: Propagate
error from arm_kprobe_ftrace()"). Restore the 'return ret;' when
arm_kprobe() fails.

Fixes: 587e8e6d640b ("kprobes: Adopt guard() and scoped_guard()")
Signed-off-by: Zhu, Yi <chuyee@google.com>
---
 kernel/kprobes.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel/kprobes.c b/kernel/kprobes.c
index bfc89083daa9..aa731b1c8897 100644
--- a/kernel/kprobes.c
+++ b/kernel/kprobes.c
@@ -1697,6 +1697,7 @@ static int __register_kprobe(struct kprobe *p)
 		if (ret) {
 			hlist_del_rcu(&p->hlist);
 			synchronize_rcu();
+			return ret;
 		}
 	}
 
